      "id": "wpf-mvvm-what-templatebinding-does",
      "topic": "wpf-mvvm",
      "subtopic": "templates-and-styles",
      "difficulty": "mid",
      "question": "What does TemplateBinding do?",
      "shortAnswer": "TemplateBinding is a lightweight binding mechanism used only inside a ControlTemplate. It binds a property of an element inside the template to a property of the control the template is applied to (the \"templated parent\").",
      "answerFrom": {
        "file": "Phase1-CSharp_And_DotNet_core_fundamental/20.WFA_and_WPF/WPF_Tutorial/12.AdvanceTopics.md",
        "section": "# But let's cover what TemplateBinding actually does, since it's a classic interview topic."
      },
      "code": {
        "lang": "xml",
        "source": "<ControlTemplate TargetType=\"local:NumericUpDown\">\n    <Border BorderBrush=\"Gray\" BorderThickness=\"1\">\n        <TextBlock Text=\"{TemplateBinding Value}\" />\n    </Border>\n</ControlTemplate>"
      },
